WEBVTT

00:00:00.455 --> 00:00:10.980
This is Lumen Reader in the terminal. It reads what your commands print, echoes what you type, and has a cursor of its own for going back over the screen.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:20.962
Run a command, and Lumen reads its output. It leaves out the command you typed, and the prompt when it comes back.

00:00:21.898 --> 00:00:23.821
Lumen Reader: ls

00:00:23.871 --> 00:00:27.590
Lumen Reader: build.sh	notes.txt	README.md	serve.sh

00:00:30.207 --> 00:00:37.454
Lumen Reader: # Weather app
A small app that shows the forecast.
Run ./build.sh to build it.
Run ./serve.sh to start the server.

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:54.086
To go back over what's there, Control-Option and the arrow keys move a review cursor by line and by word, while the shell's cursor stays put. Pressed twice, Control-Option-W spells a word, and Control-Option-Period says where you are.

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:57.100
Lumen Reader: Run ./serve.sh to start the server.

00:00:58.447 --> 00:01:00.370
Lumen Reader: Run ./build.sh to build it.

00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:03.965
Lumen Reader: A small app that shows the forecast.

00:01:05.522 --> 00:01:07.418
Lumen Reader: shows

00:01:07.468 --> 00:01:09.305
Lumen Reader: the

00:01:09.355 --> 00:01:10.960
Lumen Reader: t, h, e

00:01:11.422 --> 00:01:13.597
Lumen Reader: Line 5, column 24

00:01:14.089 --> 00:01:16.338
Lumen Reader: A small app that shows the forecast.

00:01:17.816 --> 00:01:21.891
Errors are read the same way, as soon as they appear.

00:01:24.613 --> 00:01:28.585
Lumen Reader: cat: todo.txt: No such file or directory

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:38.260
Long output is cut down to its first lines, how many more there were, and the last line, which is usually the result or the error.

00:01:40.805 --> 00:01:45.790
Lumen Reader: 1
2
3
4
195 more lines. Last line: 200

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:55.715
A full-screen program like less is announced once. After that, Lumen reads what each key changes, and says the prompt when you're back.

00:01:58.401 --> 00:02:00.016
Lumen Reader: Full screen: less

00:02:00.516 --> 00:02:02.641
Lumen Reader: Control-Option-A reads the screen

00:02:06.096 --> 00:02:09.220
Lumen Reader: - The search field keeps what you typed when you come back to it.

00:02:12.348 --> 00:02:14.613
Lumen Reader: weather-app %

00:02:14.663 --> 00:02:21.713
Output that keeps coming, like a server's log, is summed up every few seconds instead of piling up.

00:02:24.782 --> 00:02:29.140
Lumen Reader: Server listening on port 8080
GET /forecast?city=1 200 in 12 ms

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.210
Lumen Reader: 10 new lines, last: GET /forecast?city=15 200 in 12 ms

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:34.720
Lumen Reader: 10 new lines, last: GET /forecast?city=25 200 in 12 ms

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.619
Lumen Reader: 8 new lines, last: Server stopped

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:48.803
Start something slow and go to another app. When it finishes, Lumen tells you how it went, wherever you are.

00:02:51.447 --> 00:02:51.947
Lumen Reader: ./build.sh

00:02:51.906 --> 00:02:57.017
Lumen Reader: Safari, Lumen Reader test page, toolbar, show sidebar, button

00:02:57.517 --> 00:03:01.517
Lumen Reader: Show sidebar

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:06.312
Lumen Reader: Terminal: ./build.sh finished after 12 seconds

00:03:09.624 --> 00:03:17.799
The companion's Terminal section lists the commands you've run and how each one ended, with a button that takes you back to it.

00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:27.232
Lumen Reader: Lumen Reader, Terminal, Terminal: Last command: ./build.sh: finished after 12 seconds, in weather-app.

00:03:29.403 --> 00:03:36.435
